[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:fire-weapon :discharge-weapon :set-trap :spring-trap :make-kill-decision :make-harvest-timing-decision :make-fishing-execution-decision :make-hunting-execution-decision :make-gathering-execution-decision :make-trapping-execution-decision], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799006224-cloud-itonami-isco-6224-hunters-trappers-coverage" "2799006310-cloud-itonami-isco-6310-subsistence-crop-farmers-coverage" "2799006320-cloud-itonami-isco-6320-subsistence-livestock-farmers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["fire the weapon" "fired the weapon" "fires the weapon" "firing the weapon" "fire a weapon" "fired a weapon" "fires a weapon" "firing a weapon" "discharge the weapon" "discharged the weapon" "discharges the weapon" "discharging the weapon" "discharge a weapon" "discharged a weapon" "discharges a weapon" "discharging a weapon" "set the trap" "sets the trap" "setting the trap" "set a trap" "sets a trap" "setting a trap" "spring the trap" "sprang the trap" "springs the trap" "springing the trap" "sprung the trap" "spring a trap" "sprang a trap" "springs a trap" "springing a trap" "make the kill decision" "made the kill decision" "makes the kill decision" "making the kill decision" "make the harvest-timing decision" "made the harvest-timing decision" "makes the harvest-timing decision" "making the harvest-timing decision" "make the fishing execution decision" "made the fishing execution decision" "makes the fishing execution decision" "making the fishing execution decision" "make the hunting execution decision" "made the hunting execution decision" "makes the hunting execution decision" "making the hunting execution decision" "make the gathering execution decision" "made the gathering execution decision" "makes the gathering execution decision" "making the gathering execution decision" "make the trapping execution decision" "made the trapping execution decision" "makes the trapping execution decision" "making the trapping execution decision"], :adr/id 2799006340, :actor/domain :agriculture-natural-resources/subsistence-fishing-hunting-trapping-gathering-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-harvest-record :schedule-equipment-operation :flag-livelihood-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-operator :no-area :no-actuation :unknown-op :subsistence-execution-scope-excluded-op :subsistence-execution-scope-exclusion :missing-area :unknown-area :area-wrong-operator :missing-harvest-report], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "6340", :actor/wave 3, :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-livelihood-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :actor/coordination? true, :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 1000}", :test/counts "{:total 28, :assertions 110, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :operator-verification :area-verification :closed-op-allowlist :scope-excluded-op-defense-in-depth :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :livelihood-concern-always-escalate :phantom-op-hard-block], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-6340", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6340", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6340], :test/simulator :subsistenceharvest.actor-test, :db/id -1, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-6340 — Subsistence Fishing, Hunting, Trapping and Gathering Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-6340, :actor/name "Subsistence Fishing, Hunting, Trapping and Gathering Logistics Coordination Practice", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :adr/body "# ADR 2799006340: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 6340 Subsistence Fishers, Hunters, Trappers and Gatherers logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 6340\n-- Subsistence Fishers, Hunters, Trappers and Gatherers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-4 already landed: construction/metal trades 7111-7222,\nagriculture 6113/6129/6223/6224/6310/6320).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"6340\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"6340\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Subsistence Fishers, Hunters,\nTrappers and Gatherers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior\nto this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6340` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`6340` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nSubsistence Fishers, Hunters, Trappers and Gatherers take fish, game,\ntrapped animals and wild plant/animal resources primarily for\nhousehold consumption -- a domain that combines the weapons/gear and\nkill-decision concerns of ISCO 6224 (Hunters and Trappers, already\nlanded with strict guardrails) with the livelihood-vulnerability\ndimension of subsistence agriculture (ISCO 6310/6320): a\nresource-depletion or food-security risk here threatens the\nhousehold's own food supply directly, not merely a commercial outcome.\nThe controlling constraint for this vertical, given explicitly by the\ntask brief, is that this actor must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising ANY of: a decision to fire\na weapon or set/spring a trap, a fishing/hunting/gathering-execution\ndecision, or a kill/harvest-timing decision. These must be\nstructurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated\nbehind escalation. This actor is deliberately scoped to\nLOGISTICS/RECORD-KEEPING COORDINATION ONLY -- it helps log\ncatch/harvest records (post-hoc metadata only, never a\nkill/harvest-timing decision), schedule equipment maintenance, and\nsurface food-security concerns (never decides on area use, season, or\ncatch/bag limits itself).\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for STRUCTURE, and for the\ncorrect two-layer weapon/kill-decision exclusion pattern, is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6224`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6224)\n(Hunters and Trappers: `huntingtrapping.governor`'s Layer-1\nop-allowlist + Layer-2 rationale-text scan) -- cloned and read in full\nin this session and used as the direct structural template (operator/\narea provenance in place of operator/permit provenance, harvest-report\nattachment basis carried over unchanged). The livelihood-concern\nescalation pattern (op named `:flag-livelihood-concern`, ALWAYS\nescalates, never auto-commit-eligible) is adapted from\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310)\n(Subsistence Crop Farmers) -- also cloned and read in full in this\nsession.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6340` as an OSS\nlogistics/record-keeping coordination actor for subsistence fishers,\nhunters, trappers and gatherers, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Subsistence Harvest Advisor ⊣ SubsistenceHarvestGovernor** on\na `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference repos' `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **logistics/record-keeping coordination\nONLY, never weapon-firing/trap-setting/fishing-hunting-gathering-\nexecution/kill-decision authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a decision to\nfire a weapon, set/spring a trap, make a fishing/hunting/gathering-\nexecution decision, or make a kill/harvest-timing decision. These are\nnot merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent\nfrom the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-harvest-record` -- catch/harvest metadata entry (species,\n  quantity, location -- documentation only, logged AFTER the fact,\n  never a kill/harvest-timing decision)\n- `:schedule-equipment-operation` -- equipment maintenance/inspection\n  scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-livelihood-concern` -- surface a food-security/resource-\n  depletion/safety concern, ALWAYS escalates immediately, NEVER\n  auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- non-weapon equipment/supplies\n  procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles**\nfiring a weapon, setting or springing a trap, making a\nfishing/hunting/gathering-execution decision, or making a\nkill/harvest-timing decision. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:fire-weapon` or `:make-fishing-execution-decision` cannot\neven be proposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/\n`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one of the four allowlist\nops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a\nmisbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the governor's\nclosed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally\nand permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`subsistenceharvest.governor/scope-excluded-ops`) names ten\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`:fire-weapon`, `:discharge-weapon`,\n`:set-trap`, `:spring-trap`, `:make-kill-decision`,\n`:make-harvest-timing-decision`, `:make-fishing-execution-decision`,\n`:make-hunting-execution-decision`, `:make-gathering-execution-\ndecision`, `:make-trapping-execution-decision`) as defense-in-depth so\na future allowlist edit cannot silently re-open this specific\nout-of-scope path without also touching this list -- verified by\ndedicated unit tests\n(`subsistenceharvest.governor-test/hard-on-op-outside-closed-allowlist`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-even-with-otherwise-valid-fields`) and\nfive full-graph-run tests\n(`subsistenceharvest.actor-test/holds-an-attempted-weapon-firing-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-trap-setting-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-kill-decision-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-fishing-execution-decision-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-hunting-execution-decision-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-gathering-execution-decision-op`), which\nadditionally confirm the full graph run never reaches\n`commit-record!` for these ops regardless of disposition path (no\nhuman-approval path exists for a hard hold).\n\n### Eight HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Operator unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered operator (household member) record\n   (`:no-operator`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   operator is.\n2. **Area unregistered / wrong operator** -- an area-scoped proposal\n   must cite an independently registered fishing/hunting/trapping/\n   gathering area belonging to this operator\n   (`:missing-area`/`:unknown-area`/`:area-wrong-operator`). Together\n   with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that\n   a household member/gathering-area record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`, Layer 1).\n5. **Op scope-excluded** -- independently of check 4, any `:op` in the\n   ten-member `scope-excluded-ops` defense-in-depth set is a second\n   HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:subsistence-execution-scope-excluded-op`).\n6. **Subsistence-execution scope exclusion (text)** -- any proposal\n   whose free-text `:rationale` names a finalization/execution action\n   for firing a weapon, setting/springing a trap, making a\n   fishing/hunting/gathering-execution decision, or making a\n   kill/harvest-timing decision is a third HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:subsistence-execution-scope-exclusion`, Layer 2), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of checks 4\n   and 5: even if a future change somehow widened the allowlist,\n   content-based rejection still independently blocks weapon-firing/\n   trap-setting/fishing-hunting-gathering-execution/kill-decision\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n7. **Missing harvest report** -- a `:log-harvest-record` proposal with\n   no attached harvest report (`:harvest-report-attached?` false) is a\n   HARD block (`:missing-harvest-report`) -- logging a record with no\n   attached source basis is a fabricated record, not documentation,\n   mirroring `huntingtrapping.governor`'s identical check.\n8. (Checks 1-7 combined implement the CRITICAL brief's minimum HARD\n   set verbatim: household member/gathering-area provenance,\n   `:effect :propose` only, and the weapon-firing/trap-setting/\n   kill-decision structural block, PLUS the closed op-allowlist and\n   harvest-report basis carried over unchanged from the 6224\n   reference.)\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-livelihood-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to the human household\n  member, regardless of confidence (governor's implicit always-risky\n  check). This is the ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a\n  food-security/resource-depletion/safety observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the observation,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about it.\"\n  This directly implements the task's requirement that any observation\n  logged must be surfaced ONLY via an always-escalate\n  `:flag-livelihood-concern` op reviewed entirely by the human\n  household member.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds the\n  area's registered `:max-supply-order-cost` (1000 in the test\n  fixture, household scale between 6224's commercial-permit threshold\n  of 5000 and 6310's flat household threshold of 300, reflecting\n  moderately-priced subsistence gear such as nets/traps/tools;\n  inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-exact-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block: an over-threshold non-weapon supply order is not itself\n  unsafe, unlike a weapon-firing/trap-setting/fishing-hunting-\n  gathering-execution/kill-decision attempt, which is why it is\n  handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural\n  absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"weapon\", \"trap\", \"fish\", \"hunt\", \"gather\", \"kill\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nis exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a\nlogistics-coordination actor working adjacent to subsistence fishing/\nhunting/trapping/gathering necessarily discusses those concepts to do\nits record-keeping job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`subsistenceharvest.governor/subsistence-execution-scope-exclusion-\nphrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS\n(\"fire the weapon\", \"spring the trap\", \"set the trap\", \"make the\nfishing execution decision\", \"make the hunting execution decision\",\n\"make the gathering execution decision\", \"make the trapping execution\ndecision\", \"make the kill decision\", \"make the harvest-timing\ndecision\", with tense variants), never bare nouns, and\n`subsistenceharvest.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:subsistence-execution-scope-exclusion` (nor `:unknown-op` nor\n`:subsistence-execution-scope-excluded-op`). The mock advisor's own\ndefault rationale template was deliberately written to contain the\nbare nouns and negated action descriptions (\"no weapon-firing,\ntrap-setting/springing, fishing/hunting/gathering-execution or\nkill/harvest-timing decision proposed or implied\") WITHOUT containing\nany of the full finalization-action phrases, so the regression test is\na genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction,\nnot a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this session -- the\nscope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment (28 tests / 110 assertions green on the very first\n`clojure -M:test` invocation).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"6340\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6340` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-6340`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 28 tests, 110 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy), with zero mojibake found in any source or\n  doc file (`grep -c` for the UTF-8 replacement character returned 0\n  across every `.cljc`/`.clj`/`.md` file).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-harvest-timing` or\n  `:approve-fishing-execution` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to make a fishing/hunting/gathering-execution or\n  kill/harvest-timing decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (a decision to\n  take animal or plant life, or a decision that risks a subsistence\n  household's own food security), the capability itself must not\n  exist. The only op related to livelihood/compliance concerns is\n  `:flag-livelihood-concern`, which surfaces the need for human\n  household-member attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a fishing/hunting/gathering-execution or kill/harvest-timing\n  decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block: rejected -- an\n  over-threshold non-weapon supply order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  weapon-firing/trap-setting/fishing-hunting-gathering-execution/\n  kill-decision class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"weapon\" \"trap\" \"fish\"\n  \"hunt\" \"gather\" \"kill\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task, which explicitly warns the governor's\n  own scope-exclusion term list can accidentally match inside the mock\n  advisor's own default rationale text), and per the explicit\n  instruction to phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/\n  execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain\n  necessarily discusses weapon/trap/fish/hunt/gather/kill concepts to\n  do its record-keeping job (e.g. \"no weapon-firing ... proposed or\n  implied\"), so a bare-noun list would self-block the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale\n  text that deliberately contains those bare nouns,\n  `scope-exclusion-does-not-false-trip-on-bare-nouns`).\n- Modeling `area` as a single-tier unconditional check rather than the\n  `missing`/`unknown`/`wrong-operator` three-tier distinction (like\n  `huntingtrapping.permit`): rejected -- this ADR mirrors 6224\n  specifically for the two-layer exclusion pattern and provenance\n  shape, and the extra distinction gives more precise audit-ledger\n  detail (an area that does not exist vs. an area that belongs to a\n  different operator are different failure modes worth distinguishing\n  in an audited paperwork-routing system).\n- Only naming the weapon/trap/kill-decision phrases from the 6224\n  reference verbatim, omitting fishing/hunting/gathering-execution\n  phrasing: rejected per the task's explicit CRITICAL guidance, which\n  names \"a fishing/hunting/gathering-execution decision\" as a\n  distinct, additionally-forbidden category alongside weapon-firing/\n  trap-setting/kill-decision -- this vertical's broader scope (four\n  distinct subsistence activities, not just hunting/trapping) requires\n  the wider phrase and phantom-op coverage implemented here.\n- Allowing a subsistence-execution op behind a permanently-`:hard?`\n  gate that a human could still directly force via a different code\n  path (e.g. a raw store write bypassing the graph): rejected -- the\n  store protocol's only mutation entrypoints are `commit-record!`/\n  `append-ledger!`, both called exclusively from the actor graph's\n  `:commit`/`:hold` nodes, which are only reachable via `:decide`,\n  which can never route a hard violation to `:commit`; there is no\n  alternate write path in this codebase.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-harvest-record`** -- catch/harvest metadata entry (species,\n   quantity, location) only. Requires an independently registered\n   operator AND area (`:no-operator`/`:missing-area`/`:unknown-area`/\n   `:area-wrong-operator`) and an attached harvest report\n   (`:missing-harvest-report`). Not a fishing/hunting/gathering-\n   execution or kill/harvest-timing decision in any respect -- it is\n   post-hoc documentation entered AFTER the fact, never proposed or\n   implied to influence when or whether a resource is taken.\n2. **`:schedule-equipment-operation`** -- equipment maintenance/\n   inspection scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a weapon-firing/\n   trap-setting/fishing-hunting-gathering-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:subsistence-execution-scope-\n   exclusion` content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw\n   any conclusion about deploying, arming, or discharging any weapon\n   or trap, or about executing a fishing/hunting/gathering trip -- it\n   is a calendar/logistics action (e.g. scheduling a net-mending or\n   trap-line inspection slot, never scheduling a discharge, a\n   trap-spring event, or a fishing/hunting/gathering trip's\n   go/no-go decision).\n3. **`:flag-livelihood-concern`** -- surfaces a food-security/\n   resource-depletion/safety concern to the human household member;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which such\n   an observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never resolves,\n   decides, or acts on anything itself -- the human household member\n   (and, for regulatory/customary questions, the relevant authority)\n   reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- non-weapon fishing/hunting/\n   trapping/gathering-equipment supplies procurement proposal only\n   (item, cost). Not a weapon-firing, trap-setting, fishing/hunting/\n   gathering-execution or kill-decision action of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action (e.g. netting, trap-line marking tape,\n   protective gear), gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above\n   the area's registered threshold always escalates). No weapon\n   itself may be represented as the subject of this op's procurement\n   in a way that authorizes its use -- procurement coordination never\n   implies, authorizes, or schedules use.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na decision to fire a weapon, set or spring a trap, make a\nfishing/hunting/gathering-execution decision, or make a\nkill/harvest-timing decision -- these categories are structurally\nabsent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist\nitself (`subsistenceharvest.governor/op-allowlist`), (b) a second,\nindependently-named ten-member `scope-excluded-ops` defense-in-depth\nset rejected at both the governor-unit level\n(`subsistenceharvest.governor-test/hard-on-op-outside-closed-allowlist`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-even-with-otherwise-valid-fields`,\nexercising `:fire-weapon`, `:discharge-weapon`, `:set-trap`,\n`:spring-trap`, `:make-kill-decision`, `:make-harvest-timing-decision`,\n`:make-fishing-execution-decision`, `:make-hunting-execution-decision`,\n`:make-gathering-execution-decision`,\n`:make-trapping-execution-decision`) and the full-graph level\n(`subsistenceharvest.actor-test/holds-an-attempted-weapon-firing-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-trap-setting-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-kill-decision-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-fishing-execution-decision-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-hunting-execution-decision-op`,\n`.../holds-an-attempted-gathering-execution-decision-op` -- all six\nconfirm no human-approval path exists for these hard holds), and (c) a\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`subsistenceharvest.governor/subsistence-execution-scope-exclusion-\nphrases`, `.../scope-excluded-text?`), tested directly against a\nrationale that attempts to fire a weapon, spring/set a trap, make a\nfishing/hunting/gathering-execution decision, or make a\nkill/harvest-timing decision even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`subsistenceharvest.governor-test/hard-on-subsistence-execution-scope-exclusion-text`),\nand confirmed never to false-trip on routine documentation rationale\nthat legitimately contains the bare nouns \"weapon\"/\"trap\"/\"fish\"/\n\"hunt\"/\"gather\"/\"kill\" without a finalization-action phrase\n(`scope-exclusion-does-not-false-trip-on-bare-nouns`,\n`default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`)."}]